# ScholarQA-Bench, generation half: answering the questions.
#
# Pure network — the librarian plus a synthesis model over an HTTP endpoint — so
# this installs anywhere, including a laptop, and needs no GPU. The scorers are
# deliberately NOT here; they are sqa-scoring.in, which resolves against CUDA.
# That split is what lets `--skip-citation-eval` generate answers on a CPU box
# and score them somewhere else.
-r _librarian.in

